Chimera's changes to Gearcoleco 1.7.6, all build options or hooks:

- GearcolecoCore.cpp: with GEARCOLECO_FIXED_RANDOM_SEED defined, the random
  numbers that fill the console's memory at power on are not seeded from the
  host's clock. They start from the class's own fixed seed, so two runs of a
  movie start from the same memory.
- definitions.h, Input.cpp, AdamNet.cpp: a function pointer,
  gearcoleco_input_read_hook, called each time the program reads its
  controllers (Input::ReadInput) or the ADAM keyboard (a keyboard read
  through ADAMnet). It is NULL unless a frontend sets it. Chimera uses it to
  tell frames that read input from lag frames, and to run a Lua script's
  input-poll event at the moment of the read.

--- a/src/AdamNet.cpp
+++ b/src/AdamNet.cpp
@@ -474,6 +474,9 @@
             u16 transferred = 0;
             u8 code = 0;
 
+            if (gearcoleco_input_read_hook)
+                gearcoleco_input_read_hook();
+
             if ((requested > 0) && PopKey(&code))
             {
                 m_pAdam->WritePhysicalRAM(m_Transfer.buffer, code);
